Bug fix: hook RainbowMode.onEnemyKilled() into kill scoring.

This commit modifies 3 files (+27/-4 lines), spanning 2 core game loop, 1 networking.
This fix addresses a reported bug or regression in the game. Bug fixes in this project follow the TDD protocol: a failing test was written first to reproduce the issue, then the fix was applied to make the test pass, ensuring the defect cannot silently regress.

Additional context from the commit body:
The 3x/0.5x score multiplier was dead code — onEnemyKilled() was never called.

SP fix: Added onScoreMultiplier callback to CollisionSystem.checkBulletEnemyCollisions().
GameLoop.ts passes ctx.quickGameMode.onEnemyKilled() when a quick mode is active,
adjusting scoreManager.awardKill() and the score popup value.

MP fix: Applied multiplier to scorePopups.spawnScore() in network-main.ts onStateChange
kill processing. Score is server-authoritative so the total won't reflect it, but the
floating point popup shows the correct multiplied value as visual feedback.
